{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.B4CumulantBarEven","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B4CumulantBarEven","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.he4DetReduced_gt_one_at_pole","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.he4DetReduced_gt_one_at_pole","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4CumulantBarEven.lean#L147-L159","doc":"**The reduced regulator is anti-binding.**  On the pole `m·L = 1`, the\nzero-mode-reduced determinant `2(1 - m²)` exceeds `1` whenever `m² < ½` (which\nthe derived magnitude satisfies: `g_reeb² ≈ 0.1996`).  A determinant `> 1` gives\n`b = -ln det < 0` — **repulsive**.  This is the Lean-proved reason the standard\nzero-mode / reduced-determinant regularisation cannot rescue the b₄ cumulant: it\nflips the sign.  Hence the binding magnitude is not a `-ln det` free energy; the\nexact zero mode is a collective coordinate (moduli volume), i.e. the geometric\n`Vol·ρ` object, not the loop determinant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.he4DetReduced_at_pole","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.he4DetReduced_at_pole","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4CumulantBarEven.lean#L136-L139","doc":"On the pole `m·L = 1` the reduced determinant is `2(1 - m²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.he4DetReduced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.he4DetReduced","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4CumulantBarEven.lean#L131-L134","doc":"The **zero-mode-reduced** determinant — drop the vanishing `(1 - m·L)`\nfactor (the standard collective-coordinate prescription for a functional\ndeterminant with an exact zero mode). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.he4DetViaEig_zero_at_pole","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.he4DetViaEig_zero_at_pole","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4CumulantBarEven.lean#L121-L129","doc":"**Exact criticality: the A=4 determinant vanishes on the pole.**  When the\nmagnitude sits on the ss-sector pole `m·L = 1` (the derived `g_reeb` does, since\n`g_reeb² (1 + [2]_v²) = 1`, `b4_deformed_sspole_sector_probe.py`), the full A=4\nwrithe determinant is **zero** — so the single-scalar cumulant `b₄ = -ln det` is\n`+∞`.  The construction is exactly critical at the physical magnitude, not merely\nlarge: the ⁴He overshoot is this pole seen through the classical ceiling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.he4DetViaEig_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.he4DetViaEig_classical","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4CumulantBarEven.lean#L115-L119","doc":"With the classical ss eigenvalue `L² = 5`, `he4DetViaEig` is exactly the\nclassical ⁴He writhe determinant `(1 - 5m²)(1 - m²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.he4DetViaEig_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.he4DetViaEig_eq","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4CumulantBarEven.lean#L109-L113","doc":"`he4DetViaEig` collapses to the closed form `(1 - L²m²)(1 - m²)`; with\n`L² = 5` this is `he4WritheDet`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.he4DetViaEig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.he4DetViaEig","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4CumulantBarEven.lean#L101-L107","doc":"The A=4 writhe determinant written through the **ss-sector eigenvalue** `L`\n(`L² = 1 + b²`; classical integer pn-degree `b = 2` gives `L = √5`), with the\nzero mode `(1 - m·L)` factored out explicitly:\n`det(I + m·S) = (1 - m·L)(1 + m·L)(1 - m²)`.  The `(1 ± m·L)` pair is the\nspecies-**symmetric** (pp-sym, nn-sym) sector; the `(1 - m²)` is the Pauli\nintra-pair (`λ = ±1`) sector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.he4WritheDet_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.he4WritheDet_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4CumulantBarEven.lean#L89-L97","doc":"**⁴He cumulant is bar-even.**  `he4WritheDet` is a function of `m²`\nalone, so it is invariant under `m ↦ -m`.  Hence the connected cumulant\n`b₄ = -ln (he4WritheDet m)` is even in the magnitude `m`.  Under the bar\ninvolution `q ↦ q⁻¹` acting on a bar-odd magnitude (`m ↦ -m`) this says\n`b₄(q) = b₄(q⁻¹)`: bar-even symmetrisation is a **no-op** at `A = 4`, so it\ncannot tame the ⁴He magnitude overshoot (the scope-(b) obstruction to\nVector 3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.he4WritheDet_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.he4WritheDet_eq","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4CumulantBarEven.lean#L82-L87","doc":"The ⁴He writhe cumulant determinant factors as `(1 - √5 m)(1 + √5 m)(1 - m)(1 + m)`,\ni.e. it is `(1 - 5 m²)(1 - m²)` — exhibiting the symmetric `{±√5, ±1}`\nspectrum as the four roots `m ∈ {±1/√5, ±1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.he4WritheDet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.he4WritheDet","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B4CumulantBarEven.lean#L76-L80","doc":"Closed form of the ⁴He writhe cumulant determinant `det (I + m·S)`,\n`S` the `ppnn` writhe exchange matrix with spectrum `{±√5, ±1}`.  (The\n`det = this` equality is verified exactly against `mp.det` in\n`deltalambda_bareven_b4_magnitude_probe.py`.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}